---
description: Waiting UI - LabsLoading beside buttons, never inside them
globs: src/**/*.tsx
---

# Loading / waiting UI

Whenever the UI is waiting on an async action (save, restore, send, fetch,
auth, etc.), show `LabsLoading` from `@/lib/common/client`.

**Never put `LabsLoading` inside a button.** Keep the button as text only:
change the label to the action name plus three dots (`Restoring...`,
`Sending...`, `Saving...`). Render `LabsLoading` separately beside or above
the button.

```tsx
// BAD - loading component inside the button
<button disabled={busy}>
  {busy ? <LabsLoading size="sm" label="Restoring" /> : "Restore"}
</button>

// GOOD - text on the button, LabsLoading separately
{busy ? <LabsLoading size="sm" /> : null}
<button disabled={busy}>{busy ? "Restoring..." : "Restore"}</button>
```

Sizes: `sm` next to buttons / compact controls, `md` for inline panels /
lists, `lg` for full-page or centered empty states. Omit `label` on
`LabsLoading` when it sits beside a busy button (the button already names
the action). Full-page / list waits may omit a fixed label so the rotating
words show.
